{"type":"text","timestamp":1794053125613,"sessionID":"ses_e4a1d8700ffefFzRkM6prJ0N1i","part":{"id":"prt_1b5e5fd2b001UqQN0G0AqSJy70","messageID":"msg_1b5e59a55001pmN8HsNbMZTz7G","sessionID":"ses_e4a1d8700ffefFzRkM6prJ0N1i","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement a streaming RFC 4180 CSV parser as `CsvStream` in `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` with tests in `tests/test_csvstream.py`.\n- Run `python3 -m pytest -q`, report the command and actual result, then commit the work on the current branch without pushing.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6`\n- Current branch: `crew/1107-5a53f6`\n- `CsvStream` must support `delimiter=','` by default.\n- `feed(chunk)` must accept a `str` of any length and return only rows completed during that call, each row a `list[str]`.\n- The current implementation raises `TypeError` for non-`str` chunks.\n- `finish()` returns a list containing the final unterminated row if one exists, otherwise `[]`, then resets the parser for reuse.\n- Tests must therefore expect `finish()` to return a list, e.g. `[]` or `[['a', 'b']]`.\n- Parser state is instance-local: `_state`, `_row`, `_field`, `_pending_cr`, `_has_content`.\n- States are `_FIELD_START`, `_UNQUOTED`, `_QUOTED`, and `_AFTER_QUOTE`.\n- CRLF split across chunks must count as one record end; a following `\\n` after a pending `\\r` is consumed without creating another row.\n- Blank lines produce no row.\n- `\"\"` produces `['']`.\n- `a,` or `a,\\n` produces `['a', '']`.\n- Quotes inside unquoted fields are literal characters.\n- A character after a closing quote that is not a delimiter or record end raises `ValueError` from `feed` and resets state.\n- `finish()` raises `ValueError` if a quoted field is still open and resets state.\n- Do not use Python’s `csv` module.\n- Must run tests before finishing and report the exact command and actual result.\n- Must commit to the current branch with a clear message; never push or switch branches.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repository structure: existing files include `ledgerkit/money.py`, `ledgerkit/__init__.py`, and `tests/test_money.py`.\n- Confirmed clean git tree on branch `crew/1107-5a53f6` at commit `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Created `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/ledgerkit/csvstream.py` implementing `CsvStream` according to the plan.\n\n### Active\n- Need to create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/tests/test_csvstream.py`.\n- Tests should cover basic rows, multiple records per `feed`, empty middle fields, trailing delimiters, LF/CRLF/lone CR line endings, CRLF split across chunks, quoted delimiters, quoted newlines, escaped quotes, quoted empty fields, split invariance including one-character-at-a-time and quote-boundary splits, blank lines, final unterminated records, literal quotes in unquoted fields, `ValueError` cases, reuse after `finish()`, and custom delimiters.\n- Need to run `python3 -m pytest -q` from the worktree and record the actual output.\n- Need to commit `ledgerkit/csvstream.py` and `tests/test_csvstream.py` on `crew/1107-5a53f6`.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `tests/test_csvstream.py` with tests matching the implementation, especially that `finish()` returns a list of rows.\n2. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` in `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6`, fix any failures, then commit the new files on the current branch.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/ledgerkit/csvstream.py`: newly created parser implementation.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/tests/test_csvstream.py`: required test file, not yet created.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/tests/test_money.py`: existing test style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-5a53f6/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: existing package init file, currently empty.","time":{"start":1794053111083,"end":1794053125608}}}
